<title>USA: Time Warner sees cable sale deal - report.</title>
<headline>Time Warner sees cable sale deal - report.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Time Warner chairman Gerald Levin said the company would finalize deals to bring in an outside partner for New Line Cinema and sell off some cable interests by year-end, the Daily Variety said Wednesday.</p>
<p>Levin, speaking at the Variety-Schroder Wertheim Big Picture conference, also said News Corp's $2 billion satellite-TV joint venture with EchoStar Communications Corp was a &quot;form of intimidation&quot; whose &quot;true objective is to get distribution on cable of the Fox (programming) services,&quot; the report said.</p>
<p>((New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
